WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:06.240
Disease costs humanity three hundred ninety-seven point four trillion dollars annually.

2
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:11.120
That's more than global G.D.P. (one hundred and one trillion dollars).

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:18.760
The number sounds wrong because economists spent centuries measuring productivity without accounting for the people who

4
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:27.560
stopped being productive on account of being dead. The missing piece is D.A.L.Y.s (Disability-Adjusted Life Years): healthy

5
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:33.240
years deleted by disease. Die at forty instead of eighty? That's forty D.A.L.Y.s.

6
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:42.960
Spend ten years severely depressed? That's five D.A.L.Y.s. Globally: two point eight eight billion D.A.L.Y.s annually.

7
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.120
Using the commonly used one hundred fifty thousand dollar V.S.L.Y.

8
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:56.340
(value of a statistical life-year), that's three hundred eighty-two point five trillion dollars in lost human potential,

9
00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:04.200
plus eight point two trillion dollars in direct medical costs and six point seven trillion dollars in lost productivity.

10
00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.900
That's the bill. Here's the receipt for the fix: Your decentralized F.D.A.

11
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:18.180
costs forty million dollars per year to run. It saves fifty-eight point six billion dollars per year in clinical trial waste.

12
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:22.680
That's a six hundred thirty-seven to one return on R. and D.

13
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:30.320
savings alone. The total societal benefit, including lives saved, is eighty-four point eight million to one.

14
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.320
I know. Those numbers look like someone fell asleep on the keyboard.

15
00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:41.400
They didn't. Here's the breakdown. The Math: From forty-one thousand dollars to five hundred dollars.

16
00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:46.240
Traditional Phase three trials cost forty-one thousand dollars per patient.

17
00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:53.560
That's a Tesla. Per person. To find out if a pill works. The pill costs thirty-seven cents to make.

18
00:01:53.960 --> 00:02:01.860
The paperwork weighs more than the patient. Then the Oxford RECOVERY trial proved you can do the same thing for five hundred

19
00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:10.660
dollars. During a pandemic. While panicking. They tested COVID treatments on forty thousand plus patients by: Using existing

20
00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:15.200
hospital staff (revolutionary concept: doctors treating patients).

21
00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.960
Collecting data electronically (instead of sacrificing forests to the paperwork gods).

22
00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.300
Focusing on what actually matters: does the patient live or die?

23
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.560
(not "did they complete form twenty-seven-B in triplicate?").

24
00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:36.820
Your decentralized F.D.A. takes this model global. Up to forty-four point one times cost reduction.

25
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:44.260
Same data quality. Better real-world applicability. It turns out you don't need seventeen committees to answer the question

26
00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.320
"did the medicine work?". Where the fifty-eight point six billion dollars Comes From.

27
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:58.740
Global clinical trial spending is sixty billion dollars per year (and growing, because apparently inefficiency scales beautifully).

28
00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:07.160
Baseline estimate: ninety-seven point seven percent efficiency gains across the market (based on pragmatic trial cost estimates).

29
00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:13.300
This assumes pragmatic designs scale beyond simple mortality endpoints to most therapeutic areas.

30
00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:21.000
Some trial types (complex imaging, rare disease custom endpoints, device trials) won't hit that reduction.

31
00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:28.620
But the majority of spending goes to large therapeutic-area trials where RECOVERY-style designs work, and the estimate is

32
00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:35.740
conservative enough that even if a third of the market resists pragmatic redesign, the savings still dwarf the costs.

33
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:46.210
Ninety-seven point seven percent of sixty billion dollars equals fifty-eight point six billion dollars saved annually.

34
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:54.480
What fifty-eight point six billion dollars Buys You. Each new drug approval is worth an average of one point six two billion

35
00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.400
dollars in market value. The F.D.A. approves roughly fifty drugs per year.

36
00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:06.220
That is the speed at which a species with nuclear weapons and artificial intelligence has chosen to cure itself.

37
00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:13.980
Staggering. With twelve point three times more trial capacity, you could test far more treatments at once.

38
00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:22.760
With the money saved every year, you could: Fund ten thousand new pragmatic clinical trials (at five million dollars each,

39
00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:30.340
which is still luxurious by RECOVERY standards). Test treatments for seven thousand rare diseases currently ignored (because

40
00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:35.160
orphan diseases aren't profitable enough for your orphan-making economic system).

41
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:43.640
Cut drug development time from seventeen years to three to five years (most terminal patients don't have seventeen years;

42
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:52.060
this has not occurred to anyone in charge). Make medicines affordable by eliminating two point six billion dollars in development

43
00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:56.360
costs (roughly ninety percent of which is lawyers arguing about commas).

44
00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:06.660
Daily Opportunity Cost. Every day without this system costs one hundred and sixty-one million dollars in wasted trial spending

45
00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:16.660
alone. Delayed treatments cost seven point nine four billion disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y.s, healthy life-years

46
00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:25.180
over the full lag period (cumulative across all deaths and disability during the delay, not a single year's burden; yes,

47
00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:31.260
that exceeds annual global D.A.L.Y.s, because dead people keep being dead for decades).

48
00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:37.140
All because of the regulatory lag period. The lag period is not a safety feature.

49
00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.400
It is a waiting room where people die. You just gave the waiting room a nicer name.

50
00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:48.960
What It Costs to Run. Your decentralized F.D.A. costs forty million dollars per year to operate.

51
00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:54.690
Servers, engineers, compliance, global integration. The boring stuff that saves billions.

52
00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:02.420
One-time build cost is similar. For context, this is roughly what your species spends annually on Halloween costumes for

53
00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:07.460
dogs. I need you to sit with that for a moment. Less than one fighter jet.

54
00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:13.100
Less than one yacht. Less than what FIFA spends on "hospitality."

55
00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:20.720
ROI Scenarios. In the Conservative scenario, the return on investment is six hundred and thirty-seven to one, counting R

56
00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:25.180
and D savings only (net present value, or N.P.V., over ten years).

57
00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:32.500
In the Recommended scenario, the return on investment is eighty-four point eight million to one, counting R and D savings

58
00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:40.660
plus post-safety efficacy lag elimination. In the Worst case scenario, the return is an estimated sixty-six to one, counting

59
00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:48.840
higher costs and lower adoption. Even the worst case (everything goes wrong, adoption is terrible, the engineers quit and

60
00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:53.580
the servers catch fire) returns an estimated sixty-six to one.

61
00:06:54.180 --> 00:07:01.740
That beats every military investment in human history. Your worst medical outcome is still better than your best military

62
00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:05.880
one. Let that sink in while you're approving next year's defense budget.
